  "id": "COMPOUND:25206 - PROTEIN:5944",
  "verbalization": "Phelligridin A appears to interact with Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through a series of intermediate targets, including Caspase-5 and other compounds such as 5-Oxobrucine and 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol. These intermediates are all known to be targets of mitogen-activated protein kinase kinases, suggesting a potential pathway where Phelligridin A may modulate the activity of these kinases. The final scores from the three paths indicate a consistent level of confidence in the relationship, though the exact mechanism of action remains partially elucidated. The presence of multiple targets suggests that Phelligridin A may exert its effects through a complex network of signaling pathways, potentially involving caspase activation and subsequent kinase signaling. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Caspase-5 as a central node in the interaction, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise role of Phelligridin A in this process.",
